Description: 
    Implements multiBAT-combo, a multi-ancestry gene-based association testing framework that integrates GWAS summary statistics and population-specific LD information to improve gene discovery for complex traits. The package supports allele harmonisation, gene-level SNP mapping, per-gene LD matrix processing, block-diagonal joint LD construction, SVD-based multiBAT testing, and optional integration of population-specific GCTA mBAT-combo results through a weighted ACAT-based combination framework. The method is designed to aggregate association signals from genetically diverse populations, increase effective sample size, improve detection of shared gene-level associations, and avoid relying on a single LD reference for multi-ancestry data. The implementation builds on the original mBAT-combo framework developed by Ang Li.
